workedExamples.question_text:
The triangle has area $84\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find $x$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (-0.62,3.50);
\draw (O)--(P)--(Q)--cycle;
\path (O)--(P) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (O)--(Q) node[midway,left] {$x$};
\draw (0.48,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=100,radius=0.48];
\node at (0.55,0.64) {$100^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A triangle has area $43.2\text{ cm}^{2}$. Its sides of lengths $9\text{ cm}$ and $16\text{ cm}$ meet at an acute angle $\theta$. Find $\theta$ to the nearest minute.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (4,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.8,1.35);
\draw (O)--(P)--(Q)--cycle;
\path (O)--(P) node[midway,below] {$16\text{ cm}$};
\path (O)--(Q) node[midway,above left] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=36.87,radius=0.6];
\node at (0.91,0.29) {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A triangle has area $18\text{ m}^{2}$. Its sides of lengths $6\text{ m}$ and $10\text{ m}$ meet at an obtuse angle $\theta$. Find $\theta$, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (-1.68,1.26);
\draw (O)--(P)--(Q)--cycle;
\path (O)--(P) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\path (O)--(Q) node[midway,above left] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.45,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=143.13,radius=0.45];
\node at (0.18,0.70) {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An isosceles triangle has area $16\sqrt3\text{ cm}^{2}$ and apex angle $60^{\circ}$. Find the exact length $x$ of each equal side.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (L) at (-1.5,0);
\coordinate (R) at (1.5,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.598);
\draw (L)--(T)--(R)--cycle;
\path (L)--(T) node[midway,above left] {$x$};
\path (T)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\draw (-0.82,1.26)--(-0.68,1.34);
\draw (0.68,1.34)--(0.82,1.26);
\draw (-0.25,2.165) arc[start angle=240,end angle=300,radius=0.5];
\node at (0,1.82) {$60^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An isosceles triangle has area $45\text{ cm}^{2}$ and two base angles of $65^{\circ}$. Find the length $x$ of each equal side, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (L) at (-1.4,0);
\coordinate (R) at (1.4,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,3.002);
\draw (L)--(T)--(R)--cycle;
\path (L)--(T) node[midway,above left] {$x$};
\path (T)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\draw (-0.77,1.47)--(-0.63,1.53);
\draw (0.63,1.53)--(0.77,1.47);
\draw (-0.95,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=65,radius=0.45];
\draw (1.210,0.408) arc[start angle=115,end angle=180,radius=0.45];
\node at (-0.76,0.40) {$65^{\circ}$};
\node at (0.76,0.40) {$65^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

